'''Mari Illustrious''' is a [[:Category:Super Rare Cats|Super Rare Cat]] that was added in [[Version 6.10 Update|Version 6.10]] and can be unlocked by playing the [[Cat Capsule#Rare Capsule|Rare Capsule]] during the [[Neon Genesis Evangelion Collaboration Event|Evangelion Collaboration Event]].

{{Cat Info
|ID = 411
|rarity = SR
|name1 = Mari Illustrious
|name2 = Plug Suit Mari
}}

==Evolution==
Evolves into '''Plug Suit Mari''' at level 10.

==Strategy/Usage==
Mari as a unit is very similar to [[Mer-Cat (Rare Cat)|Cameraman Cat]]: both are strong against [[:Category:Floating Enemies|Floating]] enemies, but upon comparing their stats Mari is stronger in nearly every region. In spite of that, she lacks spamability and cost for what she can do, on top of being unusable in {{4c}}.

Mari won't replace Cameraman Cat against Floating because the lack of the [[Survive|Survive]] and her subpar recharge time, but is decent against Floating enemies that outrange Cameraman. She can also be useful if you don't have Mer-Cat's [[True Form]] or lack units to fight Floating enemies with. Additionally, she has the very niche use of being able to fight off Floating enemies in stages with [[Henry]], because of her marginally higher speed and Freeze Immunity.

As for general usage, she is okay but not the best, and can usually be replaced by [[Surfer Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Seafarer Cat]] and [[Weightlifter Cat (Super Rare Cat)|Pizza Cat]]. Where Mari really shines is against [[:Category:EVA Angel Enemies|EVA Angels]], as her EVA Angel Killer skyrockets her stats to [[:Category:Uber Rare Cats|Uber]] levels against them.

